<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.roster.reads ~ read the sensorium roster

Bare, the read answers every sensorium's lifecycle; `name` answers one sensorium's manifest facets.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///sense.roster.reads", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ name

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`name` params=`takes/word seat/1 as/<name> ~ the sensorium by name; absent, every one`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli · mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares sense roster

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares sense roster]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! act lar:///sense.roster.reads

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/seat spells/[[act lar:///sense.roster.reads]] ~ the seat runs it in its own process`>>
```

